  "notes": "Plugg's bounce with the lights off. The clap still lands alone on 3 and the kick still skips beats for air, but the triplet hats are thinned to a skitter and the open hats are accents instead of chains, so most of the bar is empty. What fills it is the 808: long bending slides on most phrase ends, punched in with the kick and then left to bend, and it is the one thing here that moves far. Over it sit two-note bell figures — dyads rather than chords, triads rather than ninths — repeating for two to four bars without developing. Aeolian and Phrygian are stated conventions in this scene rather than defaults, and the flat second is where the Memphis/witch-house edge comes from.",
